  "title": "Stale Pre-Vote grant from a node outside the current round's voter set panics RaftCore",
  "cause": "Pre-Vote responses are correlated only by the pre-candidate leader id, which every round started from the same local vote shares, while each round freezes its own voter set; handle_pre_vote_resp passes any matching grant to Candidate::grant_by, which expects the granter to be in that set.",
  "trigger": "A node runs a Pre-Vote round while peer P is a voter and P's grant is delayed; the voter set changes so that P is no longer a voter; the node starts another round from the same local vote (e.g. Trigger::elect(true), or the tick); P's delayed grant arrives within the RPC timeout.",
  "consequence": "grant_by's expect(\"target not in quorum set\") panics and the node's RaftCore task terminates (follower or leader; debug and release builds), so the node stops serving until restarted.",
  "sites": [
    "openraft/src/core/raft_core.rs:does_pre_candidate_vote_match",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:handle_pre_vote_resp",
    "openraft/src/proposer/candidate.rs:grant_by",
    "openraft/src/engine/engine_impl.rs:pre_elect"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "PreElect",
    "ExternalPreElect",
    "TickPreElect",
    "HandlePreVoteResponseNonMember",
    "AppendJointConfig",
    "AppendUniformConfig",
    "CommitMembership"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "PreVoteGrantFromRoundMember",
    "NoPanicOnStalePreVoteGrant"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "Two Pre-Vote rounds started from the same local vote have the same correlation key (does_pre_candidate_vote_match compares leader ids only).",
    "Each round's progress tracker contains only the voters frozen at pre_elect, and grant_by expects the granter to be one of them.",
    "The voter set can change between two such rounds without changing the local vote (leader-proposed membership change; a follower learns it by AppendEntries with an equal vote).",
    "A delayed grant can be delivered within the vote RPC timeout (election_timeout_min) after the second round started."
  ],
